{
  "name": "Triage brand mentions with AI, moderate your Juicer social wall and alert support in Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI brand mention triage\nFor social media and support teams who collect brand mentions in Juicer and want each one handled: complaints answered fast, praise shown on the website wall, spam kept off it.\n\n### How it works\n1. Juicer calls this workflow when your feed finds new posts. A first sync can bring 100+ posts, so only the newest few are processed per delivery (default 5).\n2. An OpenAI model reads each post and returns its type, urgency, a one-line summary and a suggested reply.\n3. Complaints and questions go to your support channel in Slack with the suggested reply.\n4. Praise is approved in Juicer so it shows on your social wall. Marketing gets a note.\n5. Spam is rejected in Juicer so it never shows.\n6. Every decision is logged to Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup\nAbout 15 minutes.\n\n1. In Juicer, create a feed with keyword sources for your brand and turn on the moderation queue, so new posts wait for approval.\n2. Add your Juicer API key (Developer page in Juicer) to the three Juicer nodes.\n3. Connect OpenAI, Slack and Google Sheets.\n4. Fill in **Your settings**: your support and marketing Slack channels, the cap and your log sheet URL.\n5. Activate the workflow. The trigger registers its own webhook, so n8n needs an HTTPS URL (n8n Cloud works).\n\n### Requirements\n- A Juicer account with an API key\n- OpenAI, Slack and Google Sheets accounts\n\n### Customization tips\n- Change the categories or the reply tone in **Classify the mention**.\n- Swap Slack for Microsoft Teams, Telegram or email.\n\nThis template uses the verified Juicer community node (n8n-nodes-juicer). On self-hosted n8n, install it first under Settings > Community nodes.",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "6e65c310-86b6-5b39-9e23-63b6c9477bcb",
      "name": "Overview",
